   "answer": "The three digits are for the owner, the group and others. 7 = 4 + 2 + 1 = rwx, 5 = 4 + 1 = r-x. So the owner may read, write and run the file, and the group and others may read and run it: -rwxr-xr-x. The same with letters is chmod u=rwx,go=rx script.sh.",
   "explain": "<p>On a folder the x bit means “may enter and reach the files inside”, and r means “may list the names”. A folder with r but no x lets you see names but not open the files.</p>",
