   "answer": "R is running or ready to run. S is sleeping until something happens, such as input. D is uninterruptible sleep, usually waiting for disk or network storage, and cannot be killed until the I/O ends. T is stopped, for example by Ctrl+Z. Z is a zombie: the process has ended but its parent has not collected its exit status yet.",
