   "q": "What is a zombie process, and how do you get rid of one?",
   "hint": "You cannot kill the dead.",
   "answer": "A zombie is a finished process whose entry stays in the process table because the parent has not called wait to read its exit status. It uses no memory or CPU, only a PID. kill does nothing to it, because it is already dead. Fix the parent so it waits, or end the parent: the zombie is then adopted by PID 1 (or a subreaper), which reaps it.",
   "explain": "<p>An orphan is different: a running process whose parent ended. It is adopted by PID 1 and keeps running. Many zombies can exhaust the PID limit.</p>",
