   "answer": "A physical volume (PV) is a disk or partition prepared for LVM. A volume group (VG) pools one or more PVs. A logical volume (LV) is a slice of the VG that holds a file system. To grow: add a disk with pvcreate and vgextend if the VG is full, then lvextend -r -L +20G /dev/vg0/data, where -r also grows the file system. ext4 and XFS can grow while mounted.",
